# Reference KPIs (golden master).  Hand-written from the run's own JSON
# diagnostics in the format `runTests --record` produces, then curated:
#
#   * the PHYSICAL numbers (moduli, eta, D_eff, the pellet's own geometry) are
#     pinned at 1e-6 relative -- the arithmetic is deterministic double
#     precision, so this band is about compiler and platform drift, not noise;
#   * the DEVIATION metrics (how far the numerical answer sits from the closed
#     form, the observed order of convergence) are pinned at 1e-3 relative.
#     They are small numbers, but they are DETERMINISTIC small numbers -- the
#     truncation error of a fixed scheme on a fixed grid -- so pinning them
#     is pinning the discretisation itself, and any change to the stencil
#     moves them;
#   * `newton_residual` is DELIBERATELY NOT PINNED.  It is 3.4e-15, which is
#     the round-off floor of evaluating the residual and not a property of the
#     physics; pinning cancellation round-off at a relative tolerance is what
#     column13 was re-recorded to stop doing.  What IS pinned is
#     `newton_iterations = 1`: the discretised first-order problem is LINEAR,
#     so a Newton reaches it in one step, and if that ever becomes two the
#     residual has stopped being linear in u and somebody should know.
#
